infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Mocked repo vs real Postgres: what each test can assert
  desc A mock returns your assumption; a real database returns reality
  compares
    - label Mocked repo (jest.fn)
      children
        - label ~1ms per test
          desc Single-digit ms, no Docker, runs anywhere
        - label Asserts your assumption
          desc Returns whatever you programmed it to
        - label Blind to UNIQUE / NOT NULL / CHECK
          desc No schema, so no constraint to enforce
        - label Cannot fire ON DELETE CASCADE
          desc No notion of foreign keys or referential action
        - label Migration drift invisible
          desc No schema to drift from
    - label Real Postgres (Testcontainers)
      children
        - label ~10–100ms per test
          desc Real IO, plus ~1–3s container start once per suite
        - label Asserts reality
          desc The database's actual behaviour, not your model of it
        - label Raises 23505 on a duplicate
          desc UNIQUE / FK / CHECK enforced for real
        - label Fires real cascades
          desc ON DELETE CASCADE / SET NULL reshape rows
        - label Runs the real migrations
          desc Drift fails in the test, never in prod
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
